An optional source field beneath a struct, copied to a required target
field: the _coalesce the help offers nests the field in its struct, as CUE
writes it.
-- ship/history/0.0.thema --
Schema: {
	id: string
	meta: {
		owner?: string
	}
}
-- ship/history/1.0.thema --
Schema: {
	id: string
	meta: {
		owner: string
		team:  string
	}
}

ForwardLens: (prev): {
	self: {
		id: prev.id
	}
}
-- ship/tip.thema --
Schema: {
	id: string
	meta: {
		owner: string
		team:  string
	}
}
-- out/error --
error[E0343]: meta.owner is optional in v0.0 and required in v1.0
 --> history/1.0.thema:4:3
  |
4 |         owner: string
  |         ^^^^^
  |
  = help: write meta: {owner: _coalesce(prev.meta.owner, <fallback>)} to say what to use when it is absent

error[E0346]: ForwardLens produces nothing for meta.team, which v1.0 requires
 --> history/1.0.thema:9:1
  |
9 | ForwardLens: (prev): {
  | ^^^^^^^^^^^
  |
  = help: add meta: {team: <mapping>} to self
